P?P-P!P?-6 / UNIX Version 7 (ef7c6e-main, 24 Jul 2026)

Core is 32K words.  One troff at a time, please.

/tmp is not saved and is cleared at boot. cc(1): char 8 bits,
6 per word; int and long 48. A char * is a word address plus
a byte offset.

Console in UTF-8 prints Cyrillic correctly. File names are
18 Latin characters. No vi(1) here -- ed(1) is on the system
and learn(1) will teach it.
$ tty
/dev/tty1
$ echo hello from tty1 >/tmp/two
$ 